portant indicator to be  looking at as people get vaccinated  hospitalizations  new hospitalizations daily are down  from their peak of about 18 000 people  going into the hospital each day with  covet in mid-january  eighteen thousand was the peak down to  about five thousand a day  lately again hard to feel good about  every day  five thousand people have to go into the  hospital because of covid  but it's a decline of 72 percent that is  huge  and then total cumulative people in the  hospital  at one point we had 125 000 people in  the u.s  hospitalized with covid that is down to  30  000 that's a decline in hospitalizations  of 76  so these are dramatically improving  numbers  that must continue to decline now what  about the variants  i have good news about variants the fear  is  the vaccines won't work against variants  that's been the fear  we have a new england journal of  medicine report  of the three major variants the three  major bearings are what's called the  b117 variant  that's the uk variant the b 1351 variant  that's the south african  variant and then the p1 variant which is  the brazilian  variant a study looked at  neutralization of those variants with  serum from people who have been  vaccinated fully  two pfizer doses and then you wait the  one to two weeks  the data is very good i'm putting up a  complicated image for our video audience  if if it looks confusing don't worry uh  what we are looking at here  are um these three variants i mentioned  plus two subsets of the south african  variant  all of the serum samples so the idea is  you get serum from vaccinated people  the serum has antibodies those  uh serum samples efficiently  neutralized all of the virus variants  that is really good news but let's let's  be cautious  the cautious piece is basically two  things number one  primarily with the south african variant  and secondarily with the brazilian  variant  the level of neutralization is closer to  the minimum necessary to defeat the  